### Notion Web Clipper Worker — sample requests
#
# Run the Worker locally first:
#   cd worker
#   pnpm dev                # serves http://localhost:8787
#
# These work with the REST Client (VS Code) or JetBrains HTTP client.
# `wrangler dev` reads secrets from .dev.vars (NOTION_CLIENT_ID / NOTION_CLIENT_SECRET).

@base = http://localhost:8787

### 1. CORS preflight (what the extension's browser sends first)
OPTIONS {{base}}/clip
Origin: chrome-extension://abcdefghijklmnop

### 2. OAuth token exchange
# `code` is the value Notion appends to the redirect after the user authorizes.
# `redirectUri` must match the one registered on the integration.
POST {{base}}/oauth/exchange
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "PASTE_OAUTH_CODE_HERE",
  "redirectUri": "https://abcdefghijklmnop.chromiumapp.org/"
}

### 3. Clip a page (article with extractable content)
# `accessToken` is the access_token returned by /oauth/exchange.
# `databaseId` is the id of a database shared with the integration.
POST {{base}}/clip
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "accessToken": "secret_PASTE_NOTION_ACCESS_TOKEN",
  "databaseId": "PASTE_DATABASE_ID",
  "title": "Example Domain",
  "url": "https://example.com/",
  "note": "Saved from the sample HTTP test"
}

### 4. Clip a page that won't extract (exercises the bookmark fallback)
# A login-gated / SPA URL returns no readable content, so the Worker still
# creates the page from title + url + note and responds with "fallback": true.
POST {{base}}/clip
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "accessToken": "secret_PASTE_NOTION_ACCESS_TOKEN",
  "databaseId": "PASTE_DATABASE_ID",
  "title": "My dashboard",
  "url": "https://app.example.com/private/dashboard",
  "note": ""
}

### 5. Validation error — missing required fields → 400
POST {{base}}/clip
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "accessToken": "secret_PASTE_NOTION_ACCESS_TOKEN"
}

### 6. Unknown route → 404
POST {{base}}/nope
Content-Type: application/json

{}
